  "Question": "How many whole numbers are between \\(\\sqrt{8}\\) and \\(\\sqrt{80}?\\)",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(5\\)",
    "B": "\\(6\\)",
    "C": "\\(7\\)",
    "D": "\\(8\\)",
    "E": "\\(9\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "B",
  "Solution": "Nearby perfect squares locate the endpoints without decimal approximations. Since\n\\[\n2^2=4<8<9=3^2,\n\\]\nwe have \\(2<\\sqrt8<3\\). Similarly,\n\\[\n8^2=64<80<81=9^2\n\\]\ngives \\(8<\\sqrt{80}<9\\).\n\nThus the whole numbers between the two square roots are exactly\n\\[\n3,4,5,6,7,8.\n\\]\nEvery other whole number is at most \\(2\\) or at least \\(9\\), so none is missing from this list. There are \\(6\\) numbers, choice \\(\\mathrm{B}\\).",
